.env
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Generated artifacts. All of these are fully determined by the generator plus
# a fixed --seed, so the seed is what gets committed, not the output.
#
# Committing labeled.jsonl was tempting ("it is the eval contract") and is a
# trap: the generator is still changing, and a labels file that no longer
# matches it silently scores detectors against defects the corpus does not
# contain. Regenerate instead:
#   python -m synth.generate_cfdi --n 60 --seed 1312 --out data/synth
data/
evals/datasets/*.jsonl
evals/report.json

# evals/report.md IS committed, unlike the labels above. The difference is
# whether staleness is visible: the report carries its own timestamp and seed
# in the header, so an out-of-date one announces itself. A stale labels file is
# consumed silently by the scorer and corrupts every number it produces.
